  "id": "DrugBank_DB00719 - MONDO_1040",
  "verbalization": "Azatadine is associated with Nasopharyngitis through a chain of indications that link it to Common Cold and Hydromorphone, which in turn is linked to Nasopharyngitis. This suggests that Azatadine may exert some effect that indirectly contributes to the development of Nasopharyngitis, possibly through its role in alleviating symptoms of the Common Cold. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Azatadine to Nasopharyngitis highlights a potential mechanism involving the treatment of common cold symptoms, which could have a secondary effect on nasal inflammation. The evidence supports a relationship where Azatadine may influence the body's response to cold-related conditions, potentially contributing to the development of Nasopharyngitis. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering the broader pharmacological effects of Azatadine in the context of respiratory and inflammatory conditions.",
